orAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, 5323 Harry Hines Blvd., Dallas, TX, 75390-9038, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Siegwart DJ","lastName":"Siegwart","firstName":"Daniel J","initials":"DJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3823-1931"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, 5323 Harry Hines Blvd., Dallas, TX, 75390-9038, USA."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7658-6229"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4563-5486"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8405-6743"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3823-1931"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"11","volume":"60","journalIssueId":3120247,"dateOfPublication":"2021 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2021,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Angew Chem Int Ed Engl","title":"Angewandte Chemie (International ed. in English)","essn":"1521-3773","issn":"1433-7851","isoabbreviation":"Angew Chem Int Ed Engl","nlmid":"0370543"},"printPublicationDate":"2021-03-01"},"pubYear":"2021","pageInfo":"5848-5853","abstractText":"Lipid nanoparticles (LNPs) represent the leading concept for mRNA delivery. Unsaturated lipids play important roles in nature with potential for mRNA therapeutics, but are difficult to access through chemical synthesis. To systematically study the role of unsaturation, modular reactions were utilized to access a library of 91 amino lipids, enabled by the synthesis of unsaturated thiols. An ionizable lipid series (4A3) emerged from in vitro and in vivo screening, where the 4A3 core with a citronellol-based (Cit) periphery emerged as best. We studied the interaction between LNPs and a model endosomal membrane where 4A3-Cit demonstrated superior lipid fusion over saturated lipids, suggesting its unsaturated tail promotes endosomal escape. Furthermore, 4A3-Cit significantly improved mRNA delivery efficacy in vivo through Selective ORgan Targeting (SORT), resulting in 18-fold increased protein expression over parent LNPs. These findings provide insight into how lipid unsaturation promotes mRNA delivery and demonstrate how lipid mixing can enhance efficacy.","affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, 5323 Harry Hines Blvd., Dallas, TX, 75390-9038, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"T32 GM127216","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Cancer Prevention and Research Institute of Texas","grantId":"RP190251","orderIn":0},{"agency":"American Cancer Society","grantId":"RSG-17-012-01","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NCI NIH HHS","acronym":"CA","grantId":"P30 CA142543","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIBIB NIH HHS","acronym":"EB","grantId":"R01 EB025192-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIH HHS","acronym":"NH","grantId":"T32GM127216","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institute of Biomedical Imaging and Bioengineering","grantId":"R01 EB025192-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Cystic Fibrosis Foundation","grantId":"SIEGWA18XX0","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","grantId":"T32GM127216","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIBIB NIH HHS","acronym":"EB","grantId":"R01 EB025192","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Endosomes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Inbred C57BL"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descri